<Layout title="About Jacob" description="An engineer and small-business owner sharing practical approaches to AI, automation and better systems." active="About"><article class="article"><p class="eyebrow">Hello, I'm Jacob</p><h1>Good systems should give something back.</h1><p class="lead">Time. Attention. A little less repetitive work. That is the idea behind this site.</p><h2>Engineering meets everyday work</h2><p>I have more than seven years of professional technology experience across site reliability engineering, monitoring and observability, cloud infrastructure, DevOps and automation.</p><p>I'm also a small-business owner. That gives me another reason to care about clear processes and tools that are useful without becoming a second job.</p><h2>What you'll find here</h2><p>Practical guides, small experiments and lessons about AI, technology and building better systems. I don't have every answer. I want to share useful ways to approach a problem, make the assumptions visible and improve as I learn.</p><p>The three loose themes are AI &amp; Automation, Technology &amp; Systems, and Building Smarter. They are a way to organize a small notebook, not a promise to cover everything.</p><h2>Why stockswatch.cc?</h2><p>This domain started as an investment-research experiment called StocksWatch. The focus has changed. Jacob Builds is now its home, and the old market-data desk and paid-product preview are retired.</p><p>Reusing a domain is one small way to keep the project simple. There is no investment service or financial advice offered here.</p><h2>The rule for growing</h2><p>Start small. Build something useful. Learn what people want. Add more only when there is evidence to justify the work.</p><p>This is an independent personal project. It does not speak for an employer or disclose private workplace or customer information.</p><a href="/guides">Explore the guides ↗</a></article></Layout>
